# Test Before Push

## Pre-Push Checklist

Run these steps in order before every `git push`:

### 1. Run unittest discovery
```bash
python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py" -v
```

### 2. Run pytest
```bash
python -m pytest tests/ -v --tb=short
```

All tests must pass in both runners. Do not push with failing tests.

### 2. Run pre-commit hooks
```bash
pre-commit run --all-files
```
Fix any reported issues before proceeding.

### 3. Push only if both pass
```bash
git push origin <branch>
```

---

## pre-commit Setup

If `.pre-commit-config.yaml` does not exist yet, create it:

```yaml
repos:
  - repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/pre-commit-hooks
    rev: v4.5.0
    hooks:
      - id: trailing-whitespace
      - id: end-of-file-fixer
      - id: check-yaml
      - id: check-added-large-files

  - repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit
    rev: v0.4.4
    hooks:
      - id: ruff          # lint
      - id: ruff-format   # format

  - repo: local
    hooks:
      - id: unittest
        name: unittest
        entry: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py"
        language: system
        pass_filenames: false
      - id: pytest
        name: pytest
        entry: python -m pytest tests/ --tb=short
        language: system
        pass_filenames: false
```

Install hooks once after creating the file:
```bash
pip install pre-commit
pre-commit install   # registers as a git hook going forward
```

